  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>pH of a mixture of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has to calculated</p><p>The number of equivalents of HCl is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>equivalents</mi></math></p><p>The number of equivalents of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;given is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>008</mn></math>&nbsp;equivalents</p><p>Hydrogen ion concentration of the resultant mixture is equal to<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>200</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>400</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>600</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mn>600</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>600</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>60</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>78</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
